DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These  functions  calculate the complex arc hyperbolic cosine of _z.  If
       _y _= _c_a_c_o_s_h_(_z_), then _z _= _c_c_o_s_h_(_y_).  The imaginary part of _y is chosen in
       the interval [-pi,pi].  The real part of _y is chosen nonnegative.

       One has:

           cacosh(z) = 2 * clog(csqrt((z + 1) / 2) + csqrt((z - 1) / 2))

